  "description": "ATOPOQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H135 Co4 Gd3 N2 O32 P2,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.208-3.970 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.02-114.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co4Gd3(OH)2(RPO3)2(tBuCO2)11(py)(CH3CN)(H2O)2]·CH3CN (R = 9-methyl-9H-fluoren-9-yl). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
